Voyager 3.5 documentation
==========================

This drawer is the Workbench documentation for the amigazen project
release of Voyager 3.5 (classic 68k).

The original VaporWare V3 "complete documentation" archive was
distributed from http://v3.vapor.com/ (Oliver Wagner, 2000). That
site is offline. Historical notes remain at:

  https://zapek.com/software/voyager/

Source, changelog, licence, and the full feature list for 3.5 are
in the GitHub tree and on the amigazen project site:

  https://github.com/amigazen/Voyager
  http://www.amigazen.com/voyager/

Files in this drawer
--------------------

  Readme.Docs     This file.
  voyager3docs/   VaporWare HTML manual (open main.html). Factory
                  fastlink "Docs" loads this from PROGDIR: (it
                  replaces the old www.vapor.com favourite).
  ReadMe.mui      MUI (MagicUserInterface) copyright and registration
                  notes from Stefan Stuntz. Voyager still requires MUI.
  ReadMe.TearOff  TearOff MUI classes by Szymon Ulatowski.

In the 3.5 Workbench tree
---------------------------

  V               The browser (SAS/C 68k).
  V.ReadMe        Program readme for 3.5. History for 3.4, 3.3, and
                  3.2 and older is in CHANGELOG.md in the source tree.
  Libs/           MUI classes used by Voyager.
  Plugins/        Including voyager_ssl.vlib (AmiTLS / TLS 1.2, SNI).
  Certificates/   CA bundle (cacert.pem) required for HTTPS.
  Buttons/        Toolbar imagery.
  Cache/          Disk cache (created/used at run time).

A TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library) must be running. AmiTLS
(LIBS:amitls.library) is required for HTTPS. cybergraphics.library
is opened when first needed for RTG (IsCyberModeID). Printing uses
printer.device (PRT: text, graphical bands; TurboPrint if
Turboprint: is assigned). UTF-8 HTML is mapped to the OS3 Latin-1
charmap. 

HTML manual (voyager3docs)
--------------------------

The V3 HTML documentation is in voyager3docs/

Section 8 of that manual is a historical FAQ: the 1998 Voyager FAQ
1.7 by Benjamin C. Steeves (Voyager 2.95), annotated for 3.5.
Unannotated originals are in the GitHub tree under archive/FAQ/
(English HTML, German HTML, and older .txt / AmigaGuide).

Licence
